Z||000000||Ralfy9862||02-02-2001||10:08 PM||||How exactly did you black out your tail lights i too would like to do this.||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroLisa||02-03-2001||12:41 AM||||It's the easiest thing I've ever done on my car. It's a spray tint that you put on the inside of the taillight...<BR>So, go to <A HREF="http://www.summitracing.com" TARGET=_blank>www.summitracing.com</A>  to look for their tint spray. Name is something like...Night Shade or something around there. If someone knows the name is wrong, correct me. It's the only tint spray they carry. Then take out your taillights (if by chance anyone is reading this and doesnt know how, that's easy too: lift up decklid, there are 6 little black tabs, get those off and under them are long screws. Get those out and boom, your taillights are free. Unscrew bulbs from taillight assembly and it's out.) Dissattach the red and orange covers from the clear part and start spraying the inside of the clear taillight cover. You will have to use many many coats, letting it dry in between every few.  I used almost the entire can on the GT, but I'm sure a coupe would use a bit less. I let them dry for about 24 hours in the house just to be sure. When you put your tailight assembly back in MAKE SURE you go buy some adhesive at Auto Zone or the assembly will fall out and you will be out about $130. Believe me, it will fall out, it happened to Jonathan.<BR>So if I said anything that's confusing since its way past my bedtime  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> and I Need to wake up and do the speedo on the tracer tomorrow, just reply and ask more questions  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (Sold!)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/pffsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ronnie||02-03-2001||12:55 AM||||Hey Lisa, how good does the lights shine thru after tinting them? I was worried they would be too dark.<P>------------------<BR>Black '86GT 4spd / Silver '87GT 5spd<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BOTHGTS_1.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000003||FieroLisa||02-03-2001||09:59 AM||||Well I think it is illegal in most states, but then again you don' t have to spray it on quite as dark as I did. I have never been pulled over for it, but then again I barely drive it in the winter so I wouldn't know yet.  I did stop at a gas station and have a guy tell me that I needed to replace my rear taillights bulbs because they were so dim.<P>One the GT is painted and lowered I won't be driving it any distances except to shows and hopefully will drive to those in the daytime, but it would be a concern for a daily driver.<P><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (Sold!)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/pffsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Slammed Fiero||02-03-2001||10:24 AM||||I was driving back from Lisas in August , Tinted tail lights lookin good... I stop at one exit and get something to eat , I turn too look at my car as I walk away ...wow ...what a good lookin machine!!! , 2 hours later stop for gas...walk away lookin at my car...WOW WHAT A KICK IN THE NUTS!!! the tail light was gone.... Keep in mind my car rides like a truck , you feel every little bump in the road. I haven't had any problems with police officers lookin at my rear lights. I do suggest if you black out the rears...take your time painting them. I had to get a whole new assembly from ED parks , he gave me a good price on the whole assembly , but it still hurts.<P><BR>IF you have scratches in your tail light assembly get a micro polish kit from a hobby store , you can make them like new<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
